{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1495540-storytelling-the-hedge","id":1495540,"title":"Storytelling the Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-24T18:23:06-07:00","id":1495540,"title":"Storytelling the Hedge","content":"I'm not new to Chronicles of Darkness (been running a WtF game for over a year) but I'm going to be running a CtL game for Coworkers who have never played RPGs before. My general idea is pretty simple, find a missing girl who was last seen going through a hedge gate that has been closed for the past hundred years (who knows what has changed in that time spoooooky) but I'm honestly feelings a little intimidating by the hedge, despite thinking its one of the coolest parts of CtL (obviously its one of the biggest so that tracks).<br /> <br /> Anyway, any advice on how to ST the hedge?<br /> <br /> -Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 10-24-2022, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T18:29:13-07:00","id":1495541,"title":"","content":"To elaborate, the mechanics I feel comfortable using, chases and paradigm shifts, but storytelling those mechanics is what feels intimidating to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T19:36:01-07:00","id":1495544,"title":"","content":"<b><u>1) The Hedge Abhors Never and Always</u></b><br /> <br /> The main narrative of the Hedge is that it is the place of shifting perspectives, and that the things that happen within it have the explicit goal of challenging assumptions and perspectives, towards the end of either changing their mind.....or making them break because of a dedicated rigidness. In particular, the Hedge challenges player characters (most often changelings, sometimes more human characters) in regards to those things they think they would always keep to and be, or would never commit to and be. If a character thinks stealing is always wrong, the Hedge tends to manipulate their journey to challenge that-for example, the journey might be one where in resources get stripped from them, long stretches push them physically and mentally, and finally presents them with the essentials....but not in a way up for bargain or trade. The Hedge is there to challenge who the characters are as a person, and get them to shift their narrative. Take the Hedge as an opportunity to always have character driven drama.<br /> <br /> <b><u>2) The Bark is Worse Than the Bite...</u></b><br /> <br /> This is actually more of a Changeling principle on the whole, but it really holds true with the Hedge-there's less <i>actual</i> threat in the lives of Changelings than they'd imagine. My usual standby for this is that only about 20% of the game is <i>really</i> out to ruin a character's life (being kidnapped, tortutred, killed, etc), but 50% of the game <i>looks</i> like it means them harm. For the Hedge, while it will always challenge their character, know that this means it has room to work out. It should be scary and uncertain, but the majority of what goes in just fairies getting along in their lives that makes sense to their own laws, agreements, and oaths. Never be afraid to have an escape clause ready, or to flip a threat on it's head in opposition to how it's presented.<br /> <br /> <b><u>3)...Except for when The Bite is As Bad as the Bark.</u></b><br /> <br /> That said, there is real threat in the lives of changelings. It's something you want to hold particularly true for if the Hedge wins it's Chase, the characters go into the Thorns, make bad choices that either ignore being safe and mindful of the themes of the game, and other dramatically appropriate scenarios-but even if a player character does everything right, there's still a one in five chance an encounter is actually out to be a threat to a changeling's long way home (at least, one in five if you think about in terms of the numbers I provided before). The Hedge is not a tame thing, and when it bites, allow it be terrifying.<br /> <br /> <b><u>4) The Hedge Hunts When the Players lack Drive, but Guides When They Lead</u></b><br /> <br /> The biggest thing to remember is that the Hedge primarily has it's own tools as a way of poking and prodding players who are allowing their indecision or worry to stall out the game. If the game is stalling, it's a good time to call for a roll and otherwise initiate a &quot;something rolls in/you fell into something&quot; bit of action. If, on the other hand, the players are being decisive and active in what to do after challenges, don't be afraid to let the Hedge take a back seat and otherwise make it flow easily enough from there.<br /> <br /> <b><u>5) The Hedge Reflects the Heart</u></b><br /> <br /> A good rule of thumb for portraying the Hedge to players is to just get a check on how they're feeling at the moment and what they're expecting, and then just describing the Hedge in those terms and delivering what they expect. A good simple way of gauging that steathily is just to mention something happening on a possibly adjacent road, around the corner, in the canopy, etc. that you probably wouldn't <i>normally mention</i> seperately if it were just normal scene setting, but could absolutely be normal. The general concensus of the group's response from there is a good bit to frame the &quot;mood&quot; of the Hedge going forward.<br /> <br /> <b><u>6) There's Always a Way Forward if a Price is Paid</u></b><br /> <br /> Finally, it can be tempting to make a particular moment or scene in the Hedge be an absolute chokepoint, but the Hedge is not a particularly solid barrier. If players don't want to engage with a scene or an encounter, there's a way to get around....so long as they're willing to accept the consequences. Time is the simplest cost, but since it can be a bummer to just never find the girl (unless yer group is cool with it), consider instead that going around means the Hedge takes it's price out in other ways, possibly inflicting Conditions and Tilts on the little girl that she'll have to deal with. How much is a province of your game's comfort levels and taboo subjects, and if that gets too uncomfortable, you can also consider consequences the characters themselves have to bear with-but the key is that nothing in the Hedge is meant to be the one way forward. The Hedge only closes up entirely if one refuses to engage with it entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, those are some good quick and dirty things to keep in mind for getting across the character of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-25-2022, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T18:34:27-07:00","id":1495606,"title":"","content":"This is already really helpful advice, I appreciate you a lot for taking the time to write it all up. I have a question about this one though<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1495540-storytelling-the-hedge?p=1495544#post1495544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b><u>5) The Hedge Reflects the Heart</u></b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying to say something like &quot;You hear scurrying in the trees above&quot; and then if the players say &quot;Oh its probably just some monkeys&quot; have them meet some monkey like creatures and if they say &quot;shit something is probably hunting us up there&quot; then have something be hunting them. Basically having the Hedge respond to their beliefs and ideas and emotions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T18:45:32-07:00","id":1495607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1495540-storytelling-the-hedge?p=1495606#post1495606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is already really helpful advice, I appreciate you a lot for taking the time to write it all up. I have a question about this one though<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are you saying to say something like &quot;You hear scurrying in the trees above&quot; and then if the players say &quot;Oh its probably just some monkeys&quot; have them meet some monkey like creatures and if they say &quot;shit something is probably hunting us up there&quot; then have something be hunting them. Basically having the Hedge respond to their beliefs and ideas and emotions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, you got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T20:40:59-07:00","id":1495609,"title":"","content":"